<main class="wrap">
 <a class="back" href="/projects">← All projects</a>
 <div class="meta m"><span style="color:var(--ink)">Build 02</span><span class="ln"></span><span>Distributed CI/CD platform</span><span class="ln"></span><span><span class="rec"></span>Execution core built · GitHub runtime live</span></div>

 <!-- HERO -->
 <section class="top">
  <div>
   <h1 style="font-size:clamp(76px,11.5vw,176px)">PulseGrid</h1>
   <div class="kick">“I pushed my code and it got tested.” <span>I built everything underneath that sentence.</span></div>
   <p class="lede">A lightweight distributed CI platform, like GitHub Actions or Buildkite, where I built the infrastructure myself: webhooks, a DAG workflow engine, a resource-aware scheduler, pull-based Docker workers, and leases that survive crashes.</p>
   <div class="acts"><a class="pillb solid" href="#crash">Crash a worker <span class="arr"></span></a><a class="pillb" href="#built">What's built</a><a class="pillb" href="https://github.com/VishalkiranRaichur/PulseGrid">Source</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="facts rv">
   <div><span>Role</span><span>Solo · systems design to code</span></div>
   <div><span>Like</span><span>GitHub Actions · Buildkite</span></div>
   <div><span>Core</span><span>Scheduler · Workers · Leases</span></div>
   <div><span>Tested by</span><span>Chaos demo · e2e acceptance</span></div>
   <div><span>Stack</span><span>Python · FastAPI · SQLite WAL · Docker</span></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 01 IDEA -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">01</span> · The idea</span><span>Push to result</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">The infrastructure behind CI, not the UI around it.</h2><p class="rv d1">Everyone uses CI. Few people know what happens between <b>git push</b> and a green check. I wanted to build that part myself, end to end, so every step below is real code in PulseGrid.</p></div>
  <div class="path rv">
   <div><small>01</small><b>GitHub push</b><p>A developer pushes code</p></div>
   <div><small>02</small><b>Webhook</b><p>Signature verified, retries de-duplicated</p></div>
   <div class="on"><small>03</small><b>Control plane</b><p>Finds the repo and exact commit</p></div>
   <div class="on"><small>04</small><b>Workflow DAG</b><p>Jobs with real dependencies</p></div>
   <div class="on"><small>05</small><b>Scheduler</b><p>Matches jobs to CPU, memory, GPU</p></div>
   <div><small>06</small><b>Worker</b><p>Checks out the exact SHA</p></div>
   <div><small>07</small><b>Docker</b><p>Isolated run, logs back</p></div>
   <div><small>08</small><b>Result</b><p>Back to the developer</p></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 02 PRODUCT -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">02</span> · The experience</span><span>What a developer sees</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Simple on top. Serious underneath.</h2><p class="rv d1">Connect a repo, add a small workflow file, push. From there it's a live view of every job, the machines running them and the result back on GitHub.</p></div>
  <div class="tabs rv" id="tabs"><button class="on" data-p="0"><sup>01</sup>Workflow run</button><button data-p="1"><sup>02</sup>Workers</button><button data-p="2"><sup>03</sup>On GitHub</button></div>
  <div class="screen rv">
   <span class="c tl"></span>
   <div class="hd" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:14px 34px;font-family:PM;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.16em"><span id="ptitle">PULSEGRID · WORKFLOW RUN</span><span class="lbl">CONCEPT UI · ILLUSTRATIVE DATA</span></div>
   <div class="pane on">
    <div class="run">
     <div><div class="rh"><b>Workflow #1842</b><span class="hl or">● RUNNING</span></div><div class="rm">COMMIT a31d92f · BRANCH main · ci.yml</div>
      <div class="job ok"><i>✓</i><span>lint</span><span class="t">11s</span></div>
      <div class="job ok"><i>✓</i><span>tests</span><span class="t">43s</span></div>
      <div class="job go sel"><i>●</i><span>build</span><span class="t">running · worker-b</span></div>
      <div class="job wt"><i>○</i><span>deploy</span><span class="t">waiting on build</span></div></div>
     <div><div class="m" style="color:#8f8b82">BUILD · LIVE LOGS</div><div class="logs" style="margin-top:14px"><span class="d">00:00</span> claimed by worker-b <span class="o">lease 7f3c…</span>
<span class="d">00:01</span> git checkout <span class="g">a31d92f</span> (exact SHA ✓)
<span class="d">00:02</span> docker run python:3.12-slim
<span class="d">00:02</span> mount /workspace (read-only)
<span class="d">00:04</span> pip install -r requirements.txt
<span class="d">00:19</span> building wheel…
<span class="d">00:21</span> heartbeat ✓ lease renewed
<span class="d">00:26</span> <span class="o">▌</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cap"><h4>Watch every job live</h4><p>Each run shows the exact commit, every job's state and timing, and real-time logs for any job you open.</p></div>
   </div>
   <div class="pane">
    <div class="fleet">
     <div class="wk"><div class="h"><b>Worker A</b><span class="hl" style="color:#1f7a4d">● HEALTHY</span></div><div class="bar2"><small><span>CPU</span><span>3 / 4</span></small><i><b style="width:75%"></b></i></div><div class="bar2"><small><span>MEMORY</span><span>5 / 8 GB</span></small><i><b style="width:62%"></b></i></div><div class="cur">running · tests #1843</div></div>
     <div class="wk"><div class="h"><b>Worker B</b><span class="hl" style="color:#1f7a4d">● HEALTHY</span></div><div class="bar2"><small><span>CPU</span><span>6 / 8</span></small><i><b style="width:75%"></b></i></div><div class="bar2"><small><span>MEMORY</span><span>9 / 16 GB</span></small><i><b style="width:56%"></b></i></div><div class="cur">running · build #1842</div></div>
     <div class="wk"><div class="h"><b>Worker C</b><span class="hl" style="color:var(--mut)">○ IDLE</span></div><div class="bar2"><small><span>GPU</span><span>0 / 1</span></small><i><b style="width:0"></b></i></div><div class="bar2"><small><span>MEMORY</span><span>0 / 32 GB</span></small><i><b style="width:0"></b></i></div><div class="cur">waiting for GPU jobs</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cap"><h4>See the machines</h4><p>Workers advertise CPU, memory, GPU and health. The scheduler only hands a job to a worker that can actually fit it.</p></div>
   </div>
   <div class="pane">
    <div class="gh">
     <div class="cm"><b>fix: retry flaky upload test</b><span>a31d92f · main</span></div>
     <div class="chk"><i class="or">●</i><span>PulseGrid CI — Pending</span><span class="hl" style="color:var(--mut)">ON PUSH</span></div>
     <div class="chk"><i style="color:#1f7a4d">✓</i><span>PulseGrid CI — Passed</span><span class="hl" style="color:#1f7a4d">WHEN IT FINISHES</span></div>
     <div class="chk"><i class="or">✗</i><span>PulseGrid CI — Failed</span><span class="hl or">OR THIS</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cap"><h4>Results where you work</h4><p>Status goes back to the commit on GitHub, with durable delivery: if GitHub is down, the update retries, and an old result can never overwrite a newer one.</p></div>
   </div>
   <div class="ft" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:14px 34px;font-family:PM;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--mut);border-top:1px solid var(--line)"><span>PRODUCT DIRECTION · DESIGNED FOR THIS PAGE</span><span>TODAY: API + CLI</span></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 03 CRASH SIM -->
 <section class="sec" id="crash">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">03</span> · The part I care about most</span><span>Failure handling</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Go ahead. Crash a worker.</h2><p class="rv d1">I didn't want a system that only works when everything behaves. <b>Every job runs on a lease.</b> Workers must keep renewing it with heartbeats, or PulseGrid takes the job back and gives it to someone else.</p></div>
  <div class="sim rv">
   <div class="stage">
    <div class="m" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between"><span>Job 42 · build</span><span id="clock">T+00s</span></div>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 520 330" id="simsvg">
     <rect x="190" y="20" width="140" height="56" fill="#fcfaf6" stroke="#111"/>
     <text x="260" y="44" text-anchor="middle" font-family="JO" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.5">CONTROL PLANE</text>
     <text x="260" y="62" text-anchor="middle" font-family="PM" font-size="9.5" fill="#6f6d68" id="lease">LEASE: —</text>
     <path id="la" d="M230 76 C200 140 120 160 110 220" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-dasharray="3 5"/>
     <path id="lb" d="M290 76 C320 140 400 160 410 220" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-dasharray="3 5" opacity=".25"/>
     <g id="wa" class="n_w"><rect x="40" y="220" width="140" height="70" fill="#fcfaf6" stroke="#111"/><text x="110" y="246" text-anchor="middle" font-family="JO" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.5">WORKER A</text><text x="110" y="268" text-anchor="middle" font-family="PM" font-size="9.5" fill="#6f6d68" id="wat">IDLE</text></g>
     <g id="wb" class="n_w" opacity=".35"><rect x="340" y="220" width="140" height="70" fill="#fcfaf6" stroke="#111"/><text x="410" y="246" text-anchor="middle" font-family="JO" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.5">WORKER B</text><text x="410" y="268" text-anchor="middle" font-family="PM" font-size="9.5" fill="#6f6d68" id="wbt">IDLE</text></g>
     <circle id="pulse" r="5" fill="#ff5a1f" opacity="0"/>
     <text id="x" x="110" y="214" text-anchor="middle" font-family="PM" font-size="11" fill="#ff5a1f" opacity="0">✕ CRASHED</text>
     <text id="fence" x="110" y="314" text-anchor="middle" font-family="PM" font-size="10" fill="#111" opacity="0">STALE RESULT → REJECTED</text>
    </svg>
   </div>
   <div class="ctrl">
    <div class="m">What happens</div>
    <div class="ev" data-s="1"><span>01</span><div>Worker A pulls Job 42 and gets lease <b>7f3c</b></div></div>
    <div class="ev" data-s="2"><span>02</span><div>Heartbeats renew the lease while it runs</div></div>
    <div class="ev" data-s="3"><span>03</span><div>Worker A crashes. Heartbeats stop.</div></div>
    <div class="ev" data-s="4"><span>04</span><div>Lease expires. Resources released exactly once.</div></div>
    <div class="ev" data-s="5"><span>05</span><div>Job 42 requeued, retry count +1, new lease <b>9a1e</b></div></div>
    <div class="ev" data-s="6"><span>06</span><div>Worker B runs Job 42 and finishes</div></div>
    <div class="ev fence" data-s="7"><span>07</span><div>Worker A comes back with old lease 7f3c. <b>Fenced out.</b></div></div>
    <div class="btnrow"><button class="pillb solid" id="go">Crash worker A <span class="arr"></span></button><button class="pillb" id="rs">Reset</button></div>
   </div>
  </div>
  <div class="note rv"><div class="m">Why it matters</div><p>The tricky part isn't retrying. It's making sure <b>the old worker can't come back and overwrite the new result</b>. Every heartbeat, log and completion call carries its lease ID, so a stale attempt is rejected. A chaos demo in the repo reassigns a job with a new lease after a worker expires.</p></div>
 </section>

 <!-- 04 DAG -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">04</span> · Workflows as graphs</span><span>Not a list of commands</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">It understands which job waits for which.</h2><p class="rv d1">A small YAML file becomes a <b>directed acyclic graph</b>. Lint and tests run in parallel, build waits for both, deploy waits for build. The engine decides what's ready, the scheduler decides where it fits.</p></div>
  <div class="dag rv">
<pre><span class="c"># .pulsegrid/workflow.yml</span>
<span class="k">name</span>: ci
<span class="k">jobs</span>:
  <span class="k">lint</span>:
    image: python:3.12-slim
    command: ruff check .
  <span class="k">tests</span>:
    image: python:3.12-slim
    command: pytest
  <span class="k">build</span>:
    image: python:3.12-slim
    command: python -m build
    needs: [lint, tests]
  <span class="k">deploy</span>:
    image: alpine:3.20
    command: ./deploy.sh
    needs: [build]</pre>
   <div class="g">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 460 220"><g fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.1"><rect x="20" y="40" width="90" height="38"/><rect x="20" y="140" width="90" height="38"/><rect x="190" y="90" width="90" height="38" stroke="#ff5a1f"/><rect x="350" y="90" width="90" height="38" stroke-dasharray="4 4"/><path d="M110 59 C150 59 150 109 190 109M110 159 C150 159 150 109 190 109M280 109 H350"/></g><g font-family="PM" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle"><text x="65" y="63">lint ✓</text><text x="65" y="163">tests ✓</text><text x="235" y="113" fill="#ff5a1f">build ●</text><text x="395" y="113" fill="#6f6d68">deploy ○</text></g><g font-family="PM" font-size="9" fill="#6f6d68" letter-spacing="1"><text x="20" y="28">QUEUED → DONE</text><text x="190" y="80">READY WHEN BOTH PASS</text><text x="350" y="80">BLOCKED</text></g></svg>
    <div class="rules"><div><b>NO PARENTS</b>Start queued immediately</div><div><b>HAS PARENTS</b>Blocked until every parent succeeds</div><div><b>PARENT FAILS</b>Descendants skipped, other branches keep going</div></div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 05 BUILT -->
 <section class="sec" id="built">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">05</span> · Built vs. vision</span><span>No overselling</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">The hard infrastructure already runs.</h2><p class="rv d1">The execution core and the GitHub runtime are working today. The product layer that teams would pay for comes next.</p></div>
  <div class="board rv">
   <div><h4>Built <span>08</span></h4>
    <div class="it">Control plane with durable job queue<span class="s b">LIVE</span></div>
    <div class="it">Pull-based Docker workers, CPU/memory/GPU matching<span class="s b">LIVE</span></div>
    <div class="it">Leases, heartbeats &amp; stale-worker fencing<span class="s b">LIVE</span></div>
    <div class="it">Crash recovery with retry budgets<span class="s b">LIVE</span></div>
    <div class="it">YAML workflows as a DAG<span class="s b">LIVE</span></div>
    <div class="it">Verified GitHub webhooks, no duplicate runs<span class="s b">LIVE</span></div>
    <div class="it">Exact-SHA checkout, read-only workspace<span class="s b">LIVE</span></div>
    <div class="it">Container logs to the control plane<span class="s b">LIVE</span></div></div>
   <div><h4>Next <span>06</span></h4>
    <div class="it">Commit status on GitHub with durable delivery<span class="s p">NEXT</span></div>
    <div class="it">Live dashboard &amp; real-time log streaming<span class="s p">PLANNED</span></div>
    <div class="it">Workers on separate Linux machines<span class="s p">PLANNED</span></div>
    <div class="it">Sign-in, organizations, GitHub App<span class="s p">PLANNED</span></div>
    <div class="it">Private repos &amp; encrypted secrets<span class="s p">PLANNED</span></div>
    <div class="it">Autoscaling workers<span class="s p">FUTURE</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="proof rv"><div><b>1<em>×</em></b><small>resources released exactly once on every recovery</small></div><div><b>0</b><small>duplicate workflows from GitHub retries</small></div><div><b>SHA</b><small>tests the exact pushed commit, never “latest”</small></div><div><b>Chaos</b><small>demo reassigns a job after a worker dies</small></div></div>
 </section>

 <!-- 06 ARCH -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">06</span> · Architecture</span><span>Control plane + workers</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">The brain coordinates. Workers just run.</h2><p class="rv d1">The control plane owns workflow state, scheduling, leases, retries and GitHub. Workers only provide compute and run jobs safely. <b>That split is what lets it grow from three workers to hundreds</b> without changing anything for the developer.</p></div>
  <div class="topo rv">
   <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 330">
    <rect x="300" y="10" width="400" height="76" fill="#14130f"/><text x="500" y="44" text-anchor="middle" font-family="JO" font-size="17" letter-spacing="2" fill="#fcfaf6">CONTROL PLANE</text><text x="500" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-family="PM" font-size="10" fill="#bdbab3" letter-spacing="1">STATE · SCHEDULER · LEASES · RETRIES · GITHUB</text>
    <g fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-dasharray="3 5"><path d="M440 86 C400 140 200 150 170 190"/><path d="M500 86 V190"/><path d="M560 86 C600 140 800 150 830 190"/></g>
    <text x="300" y="150" font-family="PM" font-size="9.5" fill="#ff5a1f" letter-spacing="1">PULL · HEARTBEAT</text>
    <g font-family="PM" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" letter-spacing="1">
     <rect x="80" y="190" width="180" height="120" fill="#fcfaf6" stroke="#111"/><text x="170" y="220" font-family="JO" font-size="15">WORKER A</text><text x="170" y="246" fill="#6f6d68">4 CPU · 8 GB</text><rect x="110" y="262" width="120" height="30" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-opacity=".4"/><text x="170" y="282">DOCKER</text>
     <rect x="410" y="190" width="180" height="120" fill="#fcfaf6" stroke="#111"/><text x="500" y="220" font-family="JO" font-size="15">WORKER B</text><text x="500" y="246" fill="#6f6d68">8 CPU · 16 GB</text><rect x="440" y="262" width="120" height="30" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-opacity=".4"/><text x="500" y="282">DOCKER</text>
     <rect x="740" y="190" width="180" height="120" fill="#fcfaf6" stroke="#ff5a1f"/><text x="830" y="220" font-family="JO" font-size="15">WORKER C</text><text x="830" y="246" fill="#ff5a1f">GPU · 32 GB</text><rect x="770" y="262" width="120" height="30" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-opacity=".4"/><text x="830" y="282">DOCKER</text>
    </g>
    <text x="960" y="250" font-family="PM" font-size="22" fill="#a19e97" text-anchor="middle">+</text>
   </svg>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 07 VISION -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">07</span> · The vision</span><span>What a serious CI needs</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Everything developers expect, on the same core.</h2><p class="rv d1">The production version adds the features teams rely on, plus <b>observability</b>, so when a pipeline suddenly takes ten minutes you can see why.</p></div>
  <div class="road">
   <div class="rv"><small>SECURITY</small><h5>Secrets &amp; private repos</h5><p>Encrypted secrets, private checkout, scoped GitHub App access</p></div>
   <div class="rv d1"><small>SPEED</small><h5>Caching &amp; artifacts</h5><p>Dependency and Docker-layer caches, build artifacts</p></div>
   <div class="rv d2"><small>CONTROL</small><h5>Limits &amp; rules</h5><p>Cancellation, timeouts, concurrency limits, branch rules</p></div>
   <div class="rv"><small>SCALE</small><h5>Autoscaling</h5><p>Add compute when the queue is busy, shut it down when quiet</p></div>
   <div class="rv"><small>REUSE</small><h5>Reusable workflows</h5><p>Shared pipelines across repositories</p></div>
   <div class="rv d1"><small>TEAMS</small><h5>Orgs &amp; sign-in</h5><p>Organizations, roles, repository permissions</p></div>
   <div class="rv d2"><small>INSIGHT</small><h5>Observability</h5><p>Queue depth, worker health, utilization, failure and retry rates</p></div>
   <div class="rv"><small>HISTORY</small><h5>Analytics</h5><p>Workflow duration and performance over time</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="claim rv">Not just a script that runs Docker. <span>A small, real distributed execution platform.</span></p>
  <div class="chips rv"><span>Python</span><span>FastAPI</span><span>SQLite WAL</span><span>Docker</span><span>YAML DAGs</span><span>GitHub webhooks</span><span>HMAC-SHA256</span><span>GitHub Contents API</span></div>
 </section>

